Subject: jfs_compat.h: don't redefine tid_t on substrate

Substrate's <sys/types.h> unconditionally defines tid_t (int32_t, a
thread id).  e2fsprogs's journal layer defines its own tid_t
(unsigned int, a transaction id); on substrate the two collide with a
conflicting-types error.  Skip e2fsprogs's typedef when __substrate__
is defined — the journal's tid wrap-around macros cast to int and work
regardless of the underlying type's signedness.

--- a/lib/ext2fs/jfs_compat.h
+++ b/lib/ext2fs/jfs_compat.h
@@ -31,7 +31,9 @@
 #define le64_to_cpu(x)	ext2fs_le64_to_cpu(x)
 #define be64_to_cpu(x)	ext2fs_be64_to_cpu(x)
 
+#ifndef __substrate__	/* substrate <sys/types.h> already provides tid_t */
 typedef unsigned int tid_t;
+#endif
 typedef struct journal_s journal_t;
 typedef struct kdev_s *kdev_t;
 
